s from UMBC and Zenith show him leading by about 27 points. Every major race rater labels Maryland Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put Moore's chances near 98 percent.\n\nCox faces steep structural hurdles in a state that backed Democrats by 15 points at the presidential level, and he previously lost statewide to Moore. Moore has spent the fall campaigning at home and for Democrats in other states, reflecting confidence in his standing. The main open question is turnout in a low-key race, though the size of Moore's lead makes an upset highly unlikely.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9942, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9986, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9974, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.9981, "margi